[00:10.09]What happened when the snake charmer began to play jazz? | 当耍蛇人开始吹奏爵士乐时发生了什么？
[00:16.24]As we had had a long walk through one of the markets of old Delhi, | 在穿过旧德里的一个集市走了很长一段路之后，
[00:22.01]we stopped at a square to have a rest. | 我们在一个广场上停下来休息。
[00:26.05]After a time, we noticed a snake charmer with | 过了一会儿，我们注意到广场另一头
[00:29.80]two large baskets at the other side of the square, | 有一个带着两个大筐的耍蛇人，
[00:34.06]so we went to have a look at him. | 于是就走过去看看。
[00:37.59]As soon as he saw us, | 他一见我们，
[00:39.85]he picked up a long pipe which was covered with coins and opened one of the baskets. | 就拿起了一根长长的上面镶有硬币的管乐器，并掀开了一个筐的盖子。
[00:47.11]When he began to play a tune, | 当他开始吹奏一支曲子时，
[00:49.89]we had our first glimpse of the snake. | 我们才第一次看到那条蛇。
[00:53.85]It rose out of the basket and began to follow the movements of the pipe. | 它从筐里伸出身子，随着管乐器的摆动而扭动。
[01:00.19]We were very much surprised when the snake charmer | 当耍蛇人突然开始吹奏爵士乐
[01:03.81]suddenly began to play jazz and modern pop songs. | 和现代流行歌曲时，我们都感到非常惊奇。
[01:09.41]The snake, however, continued to 'dance' slowly. | 然而，那条蛇还是慢慢地“跳”着。
[01:14.53]It obviously could not tell the difference between Indian music and jazz! | 显然，它分不清印度音乐和爵士乐！
